%T A160747 77911,101641,130425,164935,205885,254031,310171,375145,449835,535165,
%U A160747 632101,741651,864865,1002835,1156695,1327621,1516831,1725585,1955185,2206975
%N A160747 Expansion of (1 + 10*x + 20*x^2 + 10*x^3 + x^4)/(1-x)^5.
%C A160747 Ehrhart series for matroid K_4.
%C A160747 From _Chaz Reid_, Oct 16 2026: (Start)
%C A160747 a(n) is the number of 6-core partitions with n corners (Cho, Huh, Nam, and Sohn, Proposition 3.4).
%C A160747 a(n) is also the number of castle polyominoes of width 5 with n + 1 blocks, of any height (Project Euler, Problem 502: Counting Castles): columns of heights c(1), ..., c(5) >= 1 whose blocks are the maximal horizontal runs of cells, so n + 1 = c(1) + Sum_{i=2..5} max(0, c(i) - c(i-1)). In the bijection of Cho et al. (Theorem 3.3), c(i) - 1 is the number of beads in column i of the 6-abacus. (End)
%H A160747 Vincenzo Librandi, <a href="/A160747/b160747.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A160747 P. Aluffi, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1408.1702">Degrees of projections of rank loci</a>, arXiv:1408.1702 [math.AG], 2014. ["After compiling the results of many explicit computations, we noticed that many of the numbers d_{n,r,S} appear in the existing literature in contexts far removed from the enumerative geometry of rank conditions; we owe this surprising (to us) observation to perusal of [Slo14]."]
%H A160747 Hyunsoo Cho, JiSun Huh, Hayan Nam, and Jaebum Sohn, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.15554">Combinatorics on bounded free Motzkin paths and its applications</a>, arXiv:2205.15554 [math.CO], 2022. (See p. 14.)
%H A160747 J. A. De Loera, D. C. Haws and M. Koppe, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0710.4346">Ehrhart Polynomials of Matroid Polytopes and Polymatroids</a>, arXiv:0710.4346 [math.CO], 2007; Discrete Comput. Geom., 42 (2009), 670-702.
