%H A160747 <a href="/index/Rec#order_05">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (5,-10,10,-5,1).
%F A160747 G.f.: (1 + 10*x + 20*x^2 + 10*x^3 + x^4)/(1-x)^5.
%F A160747 a(n) = 1 + 7*n*(n+1)*(n^2+n+2)/4. - _R. J. Mathar_, Dec 16 2009
%F A160747 E.g.f.: (1/4)*(7*x^4 + 56*x^3 + 112*x^2 + 56*x + 4)*exp(x). - _G. C. Greubel_, Apr 26 2018
%F A160747 From _Chaz Reid_, Oct 16 2026: (Start)
%F A160747 a(n) = Sum_{k=1..5} A001263(5,k)*binomial(n+5-k, 4).
%F A160747 a(n) = Sum_{i=1..min(n,3)} A001263(n,i)*binomial(2*n+6-2*i, 2*n) for n >= 1 (Cho et al., Proposition 3.4 with t = 6).
%F A160747 a(n) = A271942(n+6, 5). (End)
%t A160747 Table[(7*n^4 + 14*n^3 + 21*n^2 + 14*n + 4)/4, {n,0,30}] (* _G. C. Greubel_, Apr 26 2018 *)
%o A160747 (Magma) [1+7*n*(n+1)*(n^2+n+2)/4: n in [0..40]]; // _Vincenzo Librandi_, Sep 18 2011
%o A160747 (PARI) a(n)=7*n*(n+1)*(n^2+n+2)/4+1 \\ _Charles R Greathouse IV_, Apr 17 2012
%Y A160747 Cf. A001263, A271942.
%Y A160747 Number of t-core partitions with n corners: A005408 (t = 3), A005891 (t = 4), A063490 (t = 5, shifted by one), this sequence (t = 6).
